WEBVTT


00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.230
When knitting points or starting
with just a few little stitches.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:09.460
We're sometimes instructed to cast on
those stitches and then increase to form

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.150
the point.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:16.190
Using a cast on rag and ravel cord makes
this process easier than just casting on

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:20.330
2-4 stitches and hoping that they
knit correctly on the first row.

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:26.330
With the rag, you can hang a weight
and ensure that the cast on knits well.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.849
Pull out the instructed number of needles.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.310
I like my crochet cast on rags, but you
can use the edge of a swatch or a small

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:36.060
piece of knitting.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.769
Anything you have laying around.

00:00:41.349 --> 00:00:48.870
Manually knit a raw forever cord, hang a
small weight, and then cast on with your

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:49.739
garment yarn.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.680
I'm using a e-wrap cast on here.

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:01.670
Now that you have a little weight in
place, you can knit that first row and

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:05.210
start increasing as
instructed in your pattern.